  "content": {
    "id": "p12-q35-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "35",
    "prompt": "The coefficient of $x$ in the expansion of $\\left(x+\\frac{1}{ax^2}\\right)^{10}$ is 15. Find the possible value(s) of $a$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$a=2$.\n\nThe $x$ term occurs at $k=3$, giving $\\frac{120}{a^3}=15$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}T_k&=\\binom{10}{k}x^{10-k}\\left(\\frac{1}{ax^2}\\right)^k\\\\T_k&=\\binom{10}{k}a^{-k}x^{10-3k}.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the $x$ term, $10-3k=1$, so $k=3$. Its coefficient is 15:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{10}{3}a^{-3}&=15\\\\\\frac{120}{a^3}&=15\\\\a^3&=8\\\\a&=2.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 62
  },
